NAME
       tree - list contents of directories in a tree-like format

SYNOPSIS
       tree [-adshfCn] [-L LEVEL] [DIRECTORY]...

DESCRIPTION
       Recursively list directories as an indented tree with line drawing
       characters, then print the number of directories and files.

OPTIONS
       -a
           show hidden files

       -d
           list directories only

       -L LEVEL
           descend at most LEVEL directories deep

       -s
           print the size of each file

       -h
           print sizes in human readable form

       -f
           print the full path of each file

       -C, -n
           force colors on or off

EXAMPLES
       tree /usr
       tree -L 2 -d /

SEE ALSO
       ls(1), find(1), du(1)
